T*
(In physical systems, dissipative frictional forces \(viscous damping proportional to) Tj
T*
(velocity F_d = - b * dx/dt\) retard motion:) Tj
T*
(* Differential Equation of Damped Harmonic Oscillator: m * \(d^2x/dt^2\) + b * \(dx/dt\)) Tj
T*
(+ k * x = 0 => d^2x/dt^2 + 2*gamma*\(dx/dt\) + omega_0^2 * x = 0, where gamma = b /) Tj
T*
(\(2*m\) is damping factor.) Tj
T*
(* Damping Regimes:) Tj
T*
(- 1. Underdamped \(gamma < omega_0\): Oscillatory decay with reduced frequency omega_d =) Tj
T*
(sqrt\(omega_0^2 - gamma^2\). Amplitude decays exponentially: A\(t\) = A_0 * e^\(- gamma * t\).) Tj
T*
(- 2. Critically Damped \(gamma = omega_0\): System returns to equilibrium in minimum) Tj
T*
(possible time without oscillation \(ideal for civil seismographs and vehicle suspension) Tj
T*
(dampers\).) Tj
T*
(- 3. Overdamped \(gamma > omega_0\): Heavy non-oscillatory creeping return to equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(* Logarithmic Decrement \(delta\): Natural log of ratio of two consecutive peak) Tj
T*
(amplitudes: delta = ln\( A_n / A_{n+1} \) = gamma * T_d = 2 * pi * gamma / omega_d.) Tj
T*
(* Quality Factor \(Q\): Dimensionless parameter measuring sharpness of resonance: Q =) Tj
T*
(2*pi * \(Stored Energy / Energy Lost per Cycle\) = omega_0 / \(2*gamma\) = pi / delta.) Tj
T*
(* Forced Oscillations and Amplitude Resonance: Under external driving force) Tj
