T*
(* 1. Magnetostriction Method \(Joule Effect\):) Tj
T*
(- Principle: When a ferromagnetic rod \(iron or nickel\) is magnetized by an alternating) Tj
T*
(magnetic field, it undergoes mechanical elastic deformation \(dimensional length change) Tj
T*
(Delta L\) irrespective of field polarity.) Tj
T*
(- Construction: Nickel rod clamped at center inside an inductive coil connected to a) Tj
T*
(high-frequency LC tank oscillator.) Tj
T*
(- Resonant Frequency: f = \(p / \(2 * L\)\) * sqrt\( Y / rho \), where p = 1,2,3... harmonic,) Tj
T*
(Y is Young's modulus, L is rod length.) Tj
T*
(- Limitation: Usable only for lower ultrasonic frequencies \(up to ~100 kHz\) due to heavy) Tj
T*
(eddy current and hysteresis losses at higher frequencies.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Piezoelectric Oscillator Method \(Curie Brothers' Effect\):) Tj
T*
(- Principle: Inverse Piezoelectric Effect. Applying an alternating RF electric field) Tj
T*
(across opposite faces of certain non-centrosymmetric crystals \(Quartz, PZT - Lead) Tj
T*
(Zirconate Titanate\) causes mechanical vibrations \(compression and rarefaction\) at) Tj
T*
(identical frequency.) Tj
T*
(- Resonant Condition: Occurs when applied RF electric frequency matches fundamental) Tj
T*
(mechanical resonant frequency of the crystal slice:) Tj
T*
(Formula: f = \(p / \(2 * t\)\) * sqrt\( Y / rho \), where t is crystal plate thickness.) Tj
T*
(- Advantages: Operates up to ultra-high frequencies \(hundreds of MHz\), highly stable,) Tj
T*
(compact.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
