([EXAMPLE 1: Resonant Frequency of Piezoelectric Quartz Plate]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: An X-cut quartz crystal plate of thickness t = 2.0 mm is used in an) Tj
T*
(ultrasonic generator. Properties of quartz are Young's modulus Y = 7.90 * 10^10 N/m^2) Tj
T*
(and density rho = 2650 kg/m^3. Calculate: \(1\) Fundamental resonant frequency f1, \(2\)) Tj
T*
(Acoustic wavelength in quartz, \(3\) Thickness required to generate ultrasound at f = 5.0) Tj
T*
(MHz.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Acoustic Velocity in Quartz v:) Tj
T*
(v = sqrt\( Y / rho \) = sqrt\( 7.90 * 10^10 / 2650 \) = sqrt\( 29,811,320.75 \) = 5460.0 m/s.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Fundamental Resonant Frequency f1 \(p = 1\):) Tj
T*
(f1 = v / \(2 * t\) = 5460.0 / \(2 * 0.002 m\) = 5460.0 / 0.004 = 1,365,000 Hz = 1.365 MHz.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Acoustic Wavelength lambda in Quartz:) Tj
T*
(lambda = v / f1 = 5460.0 / 1.365 * 10^6 = 0.004 m = 4.0 mm \(= 2 * t\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Thickness for f = 5.0 MHz:) Tj
T*
(t_new = v / \(2 * f_new\) = 5460.0 / \(2 * 5.0 * 10^6\) = 5460.0 / 10^7 = 5.46 * 10^-4 m =) Tj
T*
(0.546 mm.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Fundamental frequency = 1.365 MHz; acoustic wavelength = 4.0 mm; required) Tj
T*
(thickness for 5 MHz is 0.546 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
