([EXAMPLE 3: Ultrasonic Pulse Velocity \(UPV\) Testing of Concrete Column]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: An Ultrasonic Pulse Velocity \(UPV\) test is performed across a) Tj
T*
(reinforced concrete bridge pier of path length L = 450 mm \(0.45 m\). The measured transit) Tj
T*
(time of the ultrasonic longitudinal pulse is Delta t = 105 microseconds. Standard civil) Tj
T*
(engineering quality ratings \(IS 13311 Part 1\): v > 4.5 km/s \(Excellent\); 3.5 to 4.5 km/s) Tj
T*
(\(Good\); 3.0 to 3.5 km/s \(Medium\); < 3.0 km/s \(Doubtful\). Determine: \(1\) Ultrasonic pulse) Tj
T*
(velocity in concrete, \(2\) Dynamic Young's modulus E_d if concrete density is rho = 2400) Tj
T*
(kg/m^3 and Poisson's ratio is nu = 0.20, \(3\) Quality classification of the concrete) Tj
T*
(column.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Ultrasonic Pulse Velocity v:) Tj
T*
(v = Path Length / Transit Time = 0.450 m / \(105 * 10^-6 s\) = 4285.7 m/s = 4.29 km/s.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute Dynamic Young's Modulus E_d:) Tj
T*
(Relation for longitudinal wave in an elastic solid:) Tj
T*
(v = sqrt\( [ E_d * \(1 - nu\) ] / [ rho * \(1 + nu\) * \(1 - 2*nu\) ] \).) Tj
T*
(Rearranging: E_d = rho * v^2 * [ \(1 + nu\) * \(1 - 2*nu\) / \(1 - nu\) ].) Tj
T*
(Poisson factor = [ \(1 + 0.20\) * \(1 - 0.40\) ] / \(1 - 0.20\) = [ 1.20 * 0.60 ] / 0.80 =) Tj
T*
(0.72 / 0.80 = 0.90.) Tj
T*
(E_d = 2400 kg/m^3 * \(4285.7 m/s\)^2 * 0.90 = 2400 * \(1.8367 * 10^7\) * 0.90 = 3.967 *) Tj
T*
(10^10 N/m^2 = 39.67 GPa.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Quality Classification:) Tj
T*
(Calculated velocity v = 4.29 km/s lies between 3.5 km/s and 4.5 km/s.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Pulse velocity = 4.29 km/s; Dynamic modulus E_d = 39.67 GPa; Concrete rating) Tj
T*
(is GOOD \(satisfactory structural integrity without internal honeycombing\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
