(>> 5.7 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Explain the principle, construction, and working of a Piezoelectric Oscillator) Tj
T*
(for producing ultrasonic waves.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Principle: Inverse piezoelectric effect. When alternating RF electrical voltage) Tj
T*
(is applied across opposite metallized faces of an anisotropic crystal plate \(quartz\),) Tj
T*
(the crystal alternately expands and contracts along its optical/mechanical axis at the) Tj
T*
(driving frequency. Construction: An X-cut quartz plate is mounted between metal plates) Tj
T*
(and connected in parallel with an inductance coil L1 forming a tank circuit coupled to) Tj
T*
(the grid of a vacuum tube or transistor RF oscillator. A high-voltage DC supply powers) Tj
T*
(the circuit. Working: Tuning the variable capacitor C1 adjusts electrical frequency.) Tj
T*
(When RF frequency coincides with the natural fundamental mechanical frequency of the) Tj
T*
(crystal slice \(f = \(p/2t\)*sqrt\(Y/rho\)\), acoustic resonance occurs, radiating intense) Tj
T*
(ultrasonic waves into the adjacent medium.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the principle of Ultrasonic Pulse Velocity \(UPV\) testing in concrete) Tj
T*
(structures and its clinical engineering interpretation.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Principle: An electro-acoustic transducer placed on the concrete surface) Tj
T*
(converts high-voltage electrical pulses into longitudinal ultrasonic pulses \(~54 kHz\).) Tj
T*
(The pulse traverses concrete path length L to a receiving transducer, which reconverts) Tj
T*
(acoustic vibrations into electrical signals displayed on a digital timer. Transit time t) Tj
T*
(is recorded to compute pulse velocity v = L / t. Engineering Interpretation: Wave speed) Tj
T*
(depends directly on concrete density and elastic modulus \(v = sqrt\(E*\(1-nu\) /) Tj
T*
(rho*\(1+nu\)*\(1-2nu\)\)\). Higher velocity \(> 4.5 km/s\) indicates dense, defect-free concrete) Tj
T*
(with high compressive strength. Lower velocity \(< 3.0 km/s\) warns of internal honeycomb) Tj
T*
(voids, micro-cracks, freeze-thaw damage, or structural delamination.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
